The safety and health of every person who works here is our highest priority.

We know that the main hazards in our unit are: {{ hazards }}. We will control these hazards and prevent accidents and illness.

Our commitment: {{ commit }}

To achieve this, we will:
1. Provide and enforce the use of appropriate Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) for every job.
2. Guard all rotating and moving machine parts. Guards will not be removed during operation.
3. Maintain fire extinguishers, first aid boxes, and emergency exits — always accessible and in working condition.
4. Conduct safety training for all new workers before they start work.
5. Record and investigate every accident and near-miss — and take corrective action.
6. Conduct monthly safety inspections and share findings with the team.
7. Comply with all applicable safety laws, including the Factories Act.

No production target justifies unsafe work. Any worker can stop work if they believe it is unsafe.

